  "priorExpiration": "2004-12-22",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 2102.03 Expiration of License.\n\n(a) A license to carry pistols or revolvers that is issued in accordance with RSA 159:6 and these rules, shall have an expiration date of the later date between the following:\n\n(1) Five years from the date of issue; or\n\n(2) The last day of the month of the fifth anniversary of the license holder’s date of birth following the date of issuance.\n\nSource. #6269, eff 6-25-96; ss by #8104, INTERIM, eff 6-25-04, EXPIRES: 12-22-04; ss by #8189, eff 10-15-04; ss by #10380, eff 7-17-13; ss by #13881, eff 2-20-24 (formerly Saf-C 2102.04)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c2100.html"
